cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If this was useful in your work, please cite it."
title: "scholarcheck: literature grounding from the command line"
abstract: "Answers whether a research claim is already taken, who has extended it, and whether the references cited exist, by querying OpenAlex, Semantic Scholar, Crossref and arXiv. Withholds any negative verdict while a primary source is unreachable, so a rate-limited lookup is never reported as a fabricated citation."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Cheng
    given-names: Guo
    affiliation: "Hangzhou Institute of Medicine, Chinese Academy of Sciences, Hangzhou, China; University of Chinese Academy of Sciences, Beijing, China"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"   # fill in before the first Zenodo release
repository-code: "https://github.com/GuoCheng24/scholarcheck"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.4
keywords:
